 "response": "Driril's budget is now **$1528K**. Only Finance Office entries change the budget, and record #0001 is the only one that sets a level. Every later Finance Office increase or decrease adjusts that figure unless it has been withdrawn.\n\n**Resolving withdrawals.** A withdrawal only counts if it has not itself been withdrawn, so each chain is resolved from its last link back:\n- #0114 withdraws #0019, so #0019's withdrawal of #0004 is void and #0004 (+$237K) still applies.\n- #0566 voids #0116, which reinstates #0047. #0047 voids #0032, so #0024 (+$502K) still applies.\n- #0532 voids #0286, which reinstates #0035, so #0014 stays withdrawn.\n- #1596 voids #1006, which reinstates #0254. #0254 voids #0225, so #0214 (\u2212$571K) still applies.\n- #1039 voids #0924, which reinstates #0720. #0720 voids #0631, which reinstates #0571, so #0473 stays withdrawn.\n- The other chains work the same way. For example, #0012, #0048, #0098, #0117, #0503, #0554, #0613, #0804, #1138 and #0710 end up active. #0009, #0058, #0103, #0427, #0442, #0472, #0483 and #0678 end up withdrawn.\n\n**Summing.** All remaining active Finance Office increases and decreases from #0004 to #1600, taken in order, add up to a net change of \u2212$102K. I added well over a thousand entries by hand, so a small slip is possible.\n\n**Result:** $1630K \u2212 $102K = $1528K\n\nANSWER: $1528K",
